From 0cc9b48b512639147a2c0de5f28cf78f823741e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shahrokh <design@cariblanco.best>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 19:01:35 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 03/12] layer-split: the disk conversation tier works with a
 stage split, and the scan never deletes

Delta 1 over the upstream spill tier (#1271).

- One session file per stage plus one joint sidecar: <stem>.sess (stage 0) and
  <stem>.stage<k>.sess for each later stage; the sidecar records the stage count
  (sidecar v2; a v1 sidecar is still read). load() reads every stage file back into
  SavedConversation::stage_images, so a split spill needs no second format.
- The scan never deletes anything: a foreign identity, an unreadable sidecar, an
  orphan session file, a leftover temporary, a conversation with a missing stage
  file, and a conversation larger than the whole budget are all KEPT and counted.
  Removal lives only in the GC (enforce_budget: budget + age, oldest first, with a
  counter), and the GC leaves a conversation larger than the budget alone - removing
  it could not bring the directory under the budget.
- generate.cpp: the disk tier no longer requires stages.empty(); a disk read builds
  one SessionReadLimits per stage file, and the open log reports the kept counters.
- Tests: conversation_spill_test adds the layer-split round trip (2 stages), the
  oversized-kept case, and the orphan-kept case (76 checks).
